From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wayne Heaney <wayne.heaney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: cubie-a7s: prefer sink role on USB-C

The husb311 PD controller on port0 defaults to source role, causing it
to attempt to power the host rather than draw power from it.  With no PD
contract the board operates at the USB 2.0 default 5V/500mA, which is
insufficient under DisplayLink rendering load and causes voltage sag on
the USB host ports (hub EPROTO errors on attached devices).

Add try-power-role = "sink" so the husb311 prefers sink during PD
negotiation and accepts the host's 5V/2A offer (the existing sink-pdos
already advertise PDO_VAR up to 2A at 5V).

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -1740,6 +1740,7 @@
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 			label = "USB-C";
 			data-role = "dual";
 			power-role = "dual";
+			try-power-role = "sink";
 			op-sink-microwatt = <1000000>;
 			typec-power-opmode = "default";
